{"study_accession":"PRJNA836130","secondary_study_accession":"SRP374118","title":"MLL-AF4 cooperates with PAF1 and FACT to drive high density enhancer interactions in leukemia [RNA-seq]","description":"Aberrant enhancer activation is a key mechanism driving oncogene expression in many cancers. While much is known about the regulation of larger chromosome domains in eukaryotes, the details of enhancer-promoter interactions remain poorly understood. Recent work suggests co-activators like BRD4 and Mediator have little impact on enhancer-promoter interactions. In leukemias controlled by the MLL-AF4 fusion protein, we use the ultra-high resolution technique Micro-Capture-C (MCC) to show that MLL-AF4 binding promotes broad, high-density regions of enhancer-promoter interactions at a subset of key targets. These enhancers are enriched for transcription elongation factors like PAF1C and FACT and loss of these factors abolishes enhancer-promoter contact. This work not only provides an additional model for how MLL-AF4 is able to drive high levels of transcription at key genes in leukemia, but also suggests a more general model linking enhancer-promoter crosstalk and transcription elongation. Overall design: RNA-seq","pubmed":"37626123","geo_series":"","n_samples":4,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN28131846","study_accession":"PRJNA836130","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"polyA-RNA-seq for iALL patient sample 2","description":"polyA-RNA-seq for iALL patient sample 2","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6122646","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-08-19","attributes":[["source_name","MLL-AF4 infant ALL patient 2 blasts"],["disease","acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL)"],["treatment","not applicable"],["individual","1-year old MLL-AF4 ALL patient"],["tissue","Bone marrow aspirate"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR19136170","experiment_accession":"SRX15203352","library_layout":"PAIRED